get.description:
Return every setup-checklist item for the operator, done or not.

Response shape::

    {
        "items": [
            {
                "id": "company",
                "done": false,
                "title": "Company details",
                "message": "Missing: legal name, country.",
                "target_route": "/settings/company"
            }
        ]
    }

Unlike config-health, this always returns every registered item (never
an empty list on a healthy operator) — the checklist needs to show
completed steps too.

post.description:
Create a new operator-scoped tag.

The migration enforces:
  - per-operator name uniqueness (lower(name)) among active rows;
  - 1..64 char name length;
  - hex color format (#RRGGBB).

A duplicate-name violation surfaces as a 409.
